         The Town Clerk is the Chief Election Official: Supervises voter registration, Oversees polling places, election officers, and the general conduct of all elections.  Directs the preparation of ballots, polling places, voting equipment, and voting lists  Administers campaign finance laws,  Certifies nomination papers and initiative petitions, Serves on the Board of Registrars.  Conducts the annual town census and prepares the street list of residents. Certifies residencies The Town Clerk is the keeper of the town seal: Attests by signature and seal to bonds, contracts, bylaws, resolutions, and any other documents requiring town certification, provides certified copies of vital records,  Conducts genealogical research for members of the public, Responsible for the maintenance, disposition, and preservation of municipal archival records and materials.  Serves as the Town's Public Records Access Officer The Town Clerk is responsible for: Posting meeting agendas,  Administering the oath of office to all public officials Submitting all accepted bylaw changes to the Attorney General  Overseeing the Towns officials' compliance with the Ethics and Open Meeting Laws.  Issues marriage licenses, dog tag licenses, storage of flammables, business certificates, and raffle permits. The Wenham Town Clerk, as of April 2024, is appointed and is commissioned by the Commonwealth as a Notary Public and Justice of the Peace. 
     

 
